; Anomaly Coop - FDDA Redone (lizzardman, in GAMMA): food, drug, drink and backpack animations of the local actor. Read
; after every coop_route*.ltx (coop_route.ltx explains the order), so it wins over the generated coop_route_gamma.ltx.
;
; liz_fdda_redone_consumables creates and eats a dummy item (alife_create_item "items_anm_dummy"), so the generator
; made it host (Ruling F2-29). But its parts are not separable: liz_fdda_redone_backpack (no rule, owner by its
; callbacks) and its own file-level patches of itms_manager / ui_inventory run on a client and read the ini that only
; its on_game_load / on_option_change fill. Host-only, that ini stayed an empty table on a client: lam2 failed every
; frame in get_template_action_play_animation_fdda_config, the backpack stayed in the hands and only the move keys
; worked (live on the GAMMA stand, 2026-10-23). Owner: every machine animates its own actor. Since F2 T12 the call
; router refuses the dummy's alife_create on a client (logged), and FDDA's eat of a missing dummy is a logged no-op
; (CScriptGameObject::eat checks for nil), so nothing is duplicated.
;
; af_inspect (the artefact inspection animation of the same mod, also generated as host) is the same case (B3 audit,
; 2026-10-23): the player's own HUD animation. It puts a temporary item into the own inventory (give_object_to_actor:
; alife_create_item(.., db.actor), a request to the host that answers nil), waits for it with level.add_call and
; releases it after the animation (alife():release of an own item, a request). Host-only, ui_hud_dotmarks and
; dotmarks_main (owner) called into it and the key / update / first-update callbacks never ran on a client. The
; script locks the input (level.disable_input) until the temporary item arrives: if the host ever refuses the spawn
; the client stays locked, live check pending (see the B3 report).

[route_scripts]
liz_fdda_redone_consumables = owner
af_inspect = owner
